-- Quotation (w6): eval — APL's ⍎, constrained to what stays analyzable. Twin of w6-eval.bqn.
-- The quotation is a literal string holding one statement; anoc re-lexes it and splices the statement at parse time, so the spliced footprint is still visible to every static check (§11's conflict analysis included) — the quoted barrier below is indistinguishable from writing the line directly. Dynamic strings are a different animal (opaque footprint, interpreter territory) and are not this; templates with holes stay open in ISSUES.md.
--! registry ../registries/w6-eval.reg
--! expect damage = 23 23 8

SparkBolt , Damage += 10
eval "SparkBolt , Damage += 10"
